exit: 0
--- stdout ---
Context Optimization:
  Status: Enabled
  Active Provider: native
  Active Harnesses: claude-code, cursor, codex, kiro, kirocrew, antigravity, opencode
  Claude Code: measures only. The native PostToolUse hook leaves tool output as is, so it saves no tokens;
    Claude Code would accept a replacement (PostToolUse updatedToolOutput, built-in tools); Codex PostToolUse accepts none.
    Compact (below) shortens output by rewriting the command before it runs. Other compression needs the Headroom proxy (`headroom wrap claude`), which Downshift does not start.
  Compact: on (allowlisted shell commands run through `downshift compact`)
  Main Agent: true, Subagents: true
  Preserve Original Output: true
  Engine: in-process (built-in, standard library only)
--- stderr ---
